d States of America – Country Profile Asia Work in Bahrain – Country Profile Work in Brunei – Country Profile Work in China – Country Profile Work in Hong Kong – Country Profile Work in India – Country Profile Work in Japan – Country Profile Work in Kazakhstan – Country Profile Work in Malaysia – Country Profile Work in Qatar – Country Profile Work in Saudi Arabia – Country Profile Work in Singapore – Country Profile Work in South Korea – Country Profile Work in Turkey – Country Profile Work in United Arab Emirates – Country Profile Dubai Europe Belgium Country Profile Work in Denmark – Country Profile Work in Finland – Country Profile France Country Profile Work in Germany – Country Profile Work in Ireland – Country Profile Work in Italy – Country Profile Work in the Netherlands – Country Profile Work in Norway – Country Profile Work in Russia – Country Profile Work in Spain – Country Profile Work in Sweden – Country Profile Work in Switzerland – Country Profile Work in the United Kingdom – Country Profile Oceania Work in Australia – Country profile Work in New Zealand – Country Profile Academic Spotlight Interviews Ask a Professional PhD Guides Studentship Advice PhD Studentship Resources Vlogs Need help advertising a job? About jobs.ac.uk AI Career Advice People in Education Career Advice from jobs.ac.uk Welcome to jobs.ac.uk’s career advice section. Written by academics and professional services experts for everyone in academia and beyond. Here you can view hundreds of career articles aimed at helping you to find a job, manage your career , learn how to write a CV , find out about working abroad , get interview tips , PhD advice and much more. Don’t forget you can sign up to receive Jobs by Email to help you in your search for a new job . CV Advice How to Write a Cover Letter for Management and Administration Jobs You know you have the skills and experience an employer is looking for, yet the interview invitations never seem... > Narrative CV Guide Are you currently writing an Narrative CV? Read our guide from Katie Hoare, Careers Specialist to help you... More CV Advice Interview Tips Using AI for job applications Have you ever used AI for making job applications? Have you been able to create successful applications? More and... > Job Interview Tips: How to Prepare, Advocate for Yourself, and Play to Your Strengths as a Neurodivergent Jobseeker Job interviews can be a stressful occasion at the best of times, but when you’re neurodivergent, whether you’re autistic,... > More Interview Tips Career Development Interactive CPD Toolkit Continuing Professional Development (CPD) toolkit A Step-by-Step Guide to progress your career and record your Continuing Professional Development (CPD).... > Continuing Professional Development (CPD) in Further Education What does Continuing Professional Development (CPD) mean in Further Education, and how can it improve your practice? In this... > More Career Development Resources How to Secure Your First Postdoc Role – Webinar Registration Page Webinar Registration | 23rd September | 12:30 – 1:20 pm BST | MS Teams | Register Now >> jobs.ac.uk... > Interactive CPD Toolkit Continuing Professional Development (CPD) toolkit A Step-by-Step Guide to progress your career and record your Continuing Professional Development (CPD).... > More Resources Studentship Advice PhD Funding – A Checklist of Possible Sources Are you thinking about completing a PhD however you are not sure about funding options? In this article, Henrietta... > How to Choose Where to Do a PhD Are you looking to pursue a PhD? It’s a big adventure, and you have lots of options as you... > More Studentship Advice Country Profiles Work in China – Country Profile At just under 10 million square kilometres, China is the second-biggest country in the world by land area. In the times of the ancient dynasties, China was a leader in culture and science... Work in Germany – Country Profile Consisting of 16 states governed as a federal democracy, Germany sits at the centre of Europe and its influence on the region is keenly felt both economically and politically... More countries Primary Sidebar Follow us Latest Jobs Associate Dean for Executive Education and Enterprise, International Business School Suzhou International Business School Suzhou (IBSS), Xi'an Jiaotong - Liverpool University Location: Suzhou Salary: Competitive Law Faculty for the Centre for British Studies Centre for British Studies, Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin Location: Berlin Salary: W3 Director of Finance Leeds Beckett University Location: Leeds Salary: Competitive NIHR MDC Mixed Methods Research Fellow Grade 7/8 School of Health Sciences , University of Birmingham Location: Birmingham Salary: £36,636 - £46,049 : Grade 7, with potential progression once in post to £48,822. Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Electrical and Electronic Engineering College of Science and Engineering, University of Derby Location: Derby Salary: £38,784 - £56,535 per annum Technical Tutor in Hair Design Epsom School of Creative Business Fashion and Enterprise: Technical, University for the Creative Arts Location: Epsom Salary: £31,236 per annum pro rata Search Articles Footer Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email About Us Contact Us Terms of use Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Accessibility Statement Copyright © jobs.ac.uk 1998 - 2026 Find a Job Find PhDs Careers Advice Jobs by Email About Us Contact Us Terms of use Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Accessibility Copyright © jobs.ac.uk 1998 - 2026"
