    "https://www.jobs.ac.uk/job/DST125/postdoctoral-research-associate-in-landscape-natural-capital-accounting-and-biodiversity-reporting": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate in Landscape-natural Capital Accounting and Biodiversity Reporting",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Research Associate in Landscape-natural Capital Accounting and Biodiversity Reporting at The University of Edinburgh This site uses cookies to store information on your computer. Some of these cookies are essential, while others help us to improve your experience by providing insights into how the site is being used. For more detailed information about the cookies we use, please see our Cookie policy I Accept Cookies I Do Not Accept Cookies Necessary Cookies Necessary cookies enable core functionality such as page navigation and access to secure areas. The website cannot function properly without these cookies, and can only be disabled by changing your browser preferences. Functional Cookies These help us to personalise the website to you by remembering your preferences and settings. functional On Off Marketing Cookies Marketing cookies help us provide personalised and relevant services or advertising to our website visitors, and to assess the effectiveness of our marketing campaigns. marketing On Off Analytics Cookies Analytical cookies help us to improve our website by collecting and reporting information on its usage. analytics On Off About this tool (Opens in a new window) Skip to main content Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Recruiters Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Your Account Recruiters Back to search results Postdoctoral Research Associate in Landscape-natural Capital Accounting and Biodiversity Reporting The University of Edinburgh - CSE - School of GeoSciences - Institute for Geography and the Lived Environment Location: Edinburgh, Hybrid Salary: £41,064 to £48,822\n                                                                                        per annum (Grade 7) Hours: Full Time Contract Type: Fixed-Term/Contract Placed On: 27th August 2026 Closes: 21st September 2026 Job Ref: 14707 Full Time: 35 hours per week Fixed term: 20 th November 2027 Together we can do great things. Be part of something bigger. Here, you can continue to make a difference in everything around you. Take on new challenges, grow your career, be recognised for your contributions, and benefit from our commitment to your wellbeing. Be part of something bigger — where your work has real impact and your development matters. There are so many reasons to take your next step with us. The University of Edinburgh is a world-class organisation. We look for the best in the field across all disciplines and provide a working environment where academics can develop their careers and passion for their chosen subject area. We offer the full range of academic roles and have a genuine focus on our student’s performance and wellbeing. The opportunity: Advance urban and landscape-scale natural capital accounting and biodiversity reporting methods through action research in Scotland. We are looking for an interdisciplinary researcher with knowledge and experience in natural capital or ecosystem accounting to work within the Centre for Sustainable Forests and Landscapes on the Horizon Europe funded CircHive project until November 2027 to develop and new natural capital accounting methodologies to support urban and rural natural capital and biodiversity reporting. The post holder will co-develop and test natural capital accounts with the University of Edinburgh Forest and Peatland (FPP) landscape restoration project and the City of Edinburgh Council (CEC) to deliver useful and usable approaches to support decision-making. Your skills and attributes for success: Experience in applying natural capital concepts Experience using a range of data analysis methods Ability to communicate complex information clearly, orally and in writing Experience of working collaboratively in large, diverse teams PhD, or equivalent professional experience relevant to the role Share on social media We value your feedback on the quality of our adverts.\n            If you have a comment to make about the overall quality of this advert,\n            or its categorisation then please send us your feedback Advert information Type / Role: Subject Area(s): Location(s): Job tools Save this job Login to Save Job Max Saved Jobs Reached × Max Saved Jobs Reached A maximum of 500 Saved Jobs can be created against your account. Please remove an existing Saved Job in order to add a new Saved Job. Manage Saved Jobs × Save Job Please sign in or register for an account to save a job. Sign In Register More jobs from The University of Edinburgh Business Support Lead (Health and Wellbeing) Head of Performance Women's Rugby Applications Support Analyst Research Assistant Partnership Manager (AI Scotland) Mechanical Workshop Technician Show all jobs for this employer … More jobs like this Postdoctoral Research Assistant in Spatial Analysis of Spatial Transcriptomics for Therapy Response in Colorectal Cancer Post-Doctoral Research Fellow or Researcher Postdoctoral Research Associate in Programmable Protein-Templated Materials x4 Postdoctoral scientist Research Associate in MSK Immunology & Data Science Join in and follow us Copyright © jobs.ac.uk 1998 - 2026 Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job About Us Contact Us Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job About Us Contact Us Terms of use Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Accessibility Statement Terms of use Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Accessibility Statement Copyright © jobs.ac.uk 1998 - 2026 IE11 Trigger Browser Upgrade Recommended jobs.ac.uk has been optimised for the latest browsers. For the best user experience, we recommend viewing jobs.ac.uk on one of the following:"
