    "https://www.jobs.ac.uk/job/DSU209/project-manager-business-analyst": {
      "title": "This site uses cookies to store information on your computer.",
      "description": "Project Manager/Business Analyst at The University of Edinburgh This site uses cookies to store information on your computer. Some of these cookies are essential, while others help us to improve your experience by providing insights into how the site is being used. For more detailed information about the cookies we use, please see our Cookie policy I Accept Cookies I Do Not Accept Cookies Necessary Cookies Necessary cookies enable core functionality such as page navigation and access to secure areas. The website cannot function properly without these cookies, and can only be disabled by changing your browser preferences. Functional Cookies These help us to personalise the website to you by remembering your preferences and settings. functional On Off Marketing Cookies Marketing cookies help us provide personalised and relevant services or advertising to our website visitors, and to assess the effectiveness of our marketing campaigns. marketing On Off Analytics Cookies Analytical cookies help us to improve our website by collecting and reporting information on its usage. analytics On Off About this tool (Opens in a new window) Skip to main content Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Recruiters Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Your Account Recruiters Back to search results Project Manager/Business Analyst The University of Edinburgh - ISG - Applications Directorate - Project Services Location: Edinburgh, Hybrid Salary: £41,064 to £48,822\n                                                                                        (pro rata for part time staff) (Grade 7) Hours: Full Time Contract Type: Permanent Placed On: 1st September 2026 Closes: 18th September 2026 Job Ref: 14642 Full time: 35 hours per week Open ended (permanent) Vacancies available: 2 Join the University of Edinburgh and you’ll be making a difference to everything around you. Be part of something bigger — where you’ll do meaningful work, grow and progress, be rewarded and recognised, and benefit from our strong commitment to your wellbeing. There are so many reasons to join us. The University of Edinburgh is a world-class organisation. We are a large University covering a wide range of activities. In Professional Services, we support the University’s research and teaching, offering many career and role specialisms. The opportunity: We are looking for two enthusiastic and experienced Project Manager/Business Analysts to join Project Services which is part of the Information Services Group (ISG). We are an established specialist team of dynamic and friendly project and programme delivery professionals supporting IT and business change at the University. Working as part of our team, you will get involved with a wide variety of projects, utilising your excellent project management and business analysis skills to deliver successful outcomes for the University. Projects could include improving business efficiency, enhancing student experience, maintaining IT compliance and enabling digital transformation. The post is open-ended, and has a hybrid working pattern, involving working on campus one to two days a week and when necessary for in-person meetings and activities.  Working hours are ideally 35 hours per week, but we will consider flexible working requests. Share on social media We value your feedback on the quality of our adverts.\n            If you have a comment to make about the overall quality of this advert,\n            or its categorisation then please send us your feedback Advert information Type / Role: Subject Area(s): Location(s): Job tools Save this job Login to Save Job Max Saved Jobs Reached × Max Saved Jobs Reached A maximum of 500 Saved Jobs can be created against your account. Please remove an existing Saved Job in order to add a new Saved Job. Manage Saved Jobs × Save Job Please sign in or register for an account to save a job. Sign In Register More jobs from The 