    "https://www.jobs.ac.uk/job/DSS599/research-associate-in-superconducting-aircraft-propulsion-motors": {
      "title": "Research Associate in Superconducting Aircraft Propulsion Motors",
      "description": "Research Associate in Superconducting Aircraft Propulsion Motors at The University of Edinburgh This site uses cookies to store information on your computer. Some of these cookies are essential, while others help us to improve your experience by providing insights into how the site is being used. For more detailed information about the cookies we use, please see our Cookie policy I Accept Cookies I Do Not Accept Cookies Necessary Cookies Necessary cookies enable core functionality such as page navigation and access to secure areas. The website cannot function properly without these cookies, and can only be disabled by changing your browser preferences. Functional Cookies These help us to personalise the website to you by remembering your preferences and settings. functional On Off Marketing Cookies Marketing cookies help us provide personalised and relevant services or advertising to our website visitors, and to assess the effectiveness of our marketing campaigns. marketing On Off Analytics Cookies Analytical cookies help us to improve our website by collecting and reporting information on its usage. analytics On Off About this tool (Opens in a new window) Skip to main content Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Recruiters Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Your Account Recruiters Back to search results Research Associate in Superconducting Aircraft Propulsion Motors The University of Edinburgh - CSE - School of Engineering Location: Edinburgh Salary: £41,064 to £48,822\n                                                                                        per annum (Grade 7) Hours: Full Time Contract Type: Fixed-Term/Contract Placed On: 25th August 2026 Closes: 15th September 2026 Job Ref: 14794 Full Time: 35 hours per week Fixed term: up to 24 months The Opportunity: Develop the future of sustainable aviation Where curiosity becomes impact With roles from hospitality to research, there’s a career for everyone at the University of Edinburgh. We can offer opportunities for you to develop in your career and make a real difference in the communities around us while contributing to the world at large. The University of Edinburgh is a world-leading research-intensive university (QS ranking top 35), committed to excellence, innovation and making a positive contribution to society. As part of our diverse and inclusive community, you will work with colleagues at the SuperMachine Group and the Superconducting Electrical Futures (SEF) Lab in the School of Engineering, who share a passion for addressing global net zero challenges through superconducting technologies The School of Engineering is seeking a Postdoctoral Research Associate in Superconducting Aircraft Propulsion Motors to join a €5m Horizon Europe consortium project led by Dr Hongye Zhang at the University of Edinburgh. This 24-month, full-time role will contribute to the development of superconducting motor windings for fully electric, hydrogen fuel-cell-powered aircraft. You will undertake research involving the multiphysics modelling, design, testing and evaluation of superconducting propulsion motor technologies. You will work closely with Dr Hongye Zhang and EU/UK academic/industrial partners across the project consortium, contributing to project milestones, technical reports, publications and presentations. We are looking for a highly motivated researcher with a PhD, or equivalent experience, in electrical engineering, mechanical engineering, thermal engineering, aerospace engineering, physics or a related discipline. You should have strong analytical and research skills, together with knowledge or experience relevant to electric machines, applied superconductivity, or aerospace technologies. Experience with electro-mechanical-thermal modelling, cryogenic systems, superconducting materials, motor windings or hydrogen-electric propulsion would be advantageous. The role offers an opportunity to contribute to internationally significant research addressing the transition to cleaner aviation. Occasional travel to consortium meetings, conferences or partner facilities may be required. Laboratory work may involve cryogenic liquids, including liquid nitrogen, and will be supported by appropriate training and risk assessments. We encourage applications from candidates with diverse backgrounds and experiences who can contribute to our values of excellence, integrity, inclusion, relevance and ambition. Apply now to join the project team and help develop innovative propulsion technologies for the future of sustainable aviation. A career with us has a range of other benefits that can be tailored to your lifestyle, including: A competitive pension scheme Generous annual leave allowance Staff discounts and a wide range of health and wellbeing support Professional development and training opportunities Family-friendly and inclusive policies Employee networks and support for a diverse and welcoming community Share on social media We value your feedback on the quality of our adverts.\n            If you have a comment to make about the overall quality of this advert,\n            or its categorisation then please send us your feedback Advert information Type / Role: Subject Area(s): Location(s): Job tools Save this job Login to Save Job Max Saved Jobs Reached × Max Saved Jobs Reached A maximum of 500 Saved Jobs can be created against your account. Please remove an existing Saved Job in order to add a new Saved Job. Manage Saved Jobs × Save Job Please sign in or register for an account to save a job. Sign In Register More jobs from The University of Edinburgh Business Support Lead (Health and Wellbeing) Head of Performance Women's Rugby Applications Support Analyst Research Assistant Partnership Manager (AI Scotland) Mechanical Workshop Technician Show all jobs for this employer … More jobs like this Postdoctoral Research Associate in Programmable Protein-Templated Materials x4 Research Associate (AI-Enhanced Predictive Modelling and Optimisation) Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Electrical and Electronic Engineering Research Associate/Senior Research Associate in Control for Soft Robot Wearable Assistance Research Fellow in Quantum Algorithms for Chemical Reaction Networks (828923) Join in and follow us Copyright © jobs.ac.uk 1998 - 2026 Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job About Us Contact Us Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job About Us Contact Us Terms of use Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Accessibility Statement Terms of use Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Accessibility Statement Copyright © jobs.ac.uk 1998 - 2026 IE11 Trigger Browser Upgrade Recommended jobs.ac.uk has been optimised for the latest browsers. For the best user experience, we recommend viewing jobs.ac.uk on one of the following:"
