    "https://www.jobs.ac.uk/job/DSS594/knowledge-manager": {
      "title": "This site uses cookies to store information on your computer.",
      "description": "Knowledge Manager at The University of Edinburgh This site uses cookies to store information on your computer. Some of these cookies are essential, while others help us to improve your experience by providing insights into how the site is being used. For more detailed information about the cookies we use, please see our Cookie policy I Accept Cookies I Do Not Accept Cookies Necessary Cookies Necessary cookies enable core functionality such as page navigation and access to secure areas. The website cannot function properly without these cookies, and can only be disabled by changing your browser preferences. Functional Cookies These help us to personalise the website to you by remembering your preferences and settings. functional On Off Marketing Cookies Marketing cookies help us provide personalised and relevant services or advertising to our website visitors, and to assess the effectiveness of our marketing campaigns. marketing On Off Analytics Cookies Analytical cookies help us to improve our website by collecting and reporting information on its usage. analytics On Off About this tool (Opens in a new window) Skip to main content Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Recruiters Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Your Account Recruiters Back to search results Knowledge Manager The University of Edinburgh - Information Services Group - User Services Directorate - IT Services Team Location: Edinburgh, Hybrid Salary: £41,064 to £48,822\n                                                                                        per annum (pro rata for part time staff) (Grade 7) Hours: Full Time Contract Type: Fixed-Term/Contract Placed On: 25th August 2026 Closes: 8th September 2026 Job Ref: 14651 Full time: 35 hours per week (working pattern is Monday – Friday - 09:00-17:00) Fixed term: 12 months The opportunity: We’re looking for a Knowledge Manager to join our IT Services team who operate within the User Services Directorate as part of Operational Services. This is an exciting role central to the ongoing development of our Knowledge Management strategy for IT, Library and eLearning Services at the University of Edinburgh. Part of a small team you will be responsible for the development, implementation and continual improvement of our Knowledge Management processes and Self-Service tools including our AskEdHelp Service, a chatbot designed inhouse to deliver Self Service support to our students. You will also work with other Subject Matter Experts to deliver advice and support for IT Service Management activities. This is a great opportunity to be involved in shaping the next generation of support services at the University of Edinburgh by defining our Knowledge Management strategy and collaborating with colleagues to deliver cutting edge solutions enabling our users to get help in the way they want, when they want. The post holder will define the Knowledge Management strategy and lead the content design and development of services. They will create guidelines for what information is captured and by who, and they will monitor the process to ensure it is working effectively. The post holder will provide analytical insights, identify trends and use this information to drive service improvement. They will be responsible for the Knowledge Management toolset and ensure it meets the strategic aims of the University. They will recommend and assist in the development of new knowledge tools that enhance the user experience including our chatbots and knowledgebase content management. A career with us has a range of other benefits that can be tailored to your lifestyle: Opportunities to develop new skills and broaden your experience Flexible/hybrid where the roles allow Variety every day Excellent benefits and support Share on social media We value your feedback on the quality of our adverts.\n            If you have a comment to make about the overall quality of this advert,\n            or its categorisation then please send us your feedback Advert information Type / Role: Subject Area(s): Location(s): Job tools Save this job Login to Save Job Max Saved Jobs Reached × Max Saved Jobs Reached A maximum of 500 Saved Jobs can be created against your account. Please remove an existing Saved Job in order to add a new Saved Job. Manage Saved Jobs × Save Job Please sign in or register for an account to save a job. Sign In Register More jobs from The University of Edinburgh Business Support Lead (Health and Wellbeing) Head of Performance Women's Rugby Applications Support Analyst Research Assistant Partnership Manager (AI Scotland) Mechanical Workshop Technician Show all jobs for this employer … More jobs like this Communications and Marketing Project Manager Project and Impact Manager (Energy and Health) Copywriter Associate Dean for Executive Education and Enterprise, International Business School Suzhou Deputy Director (Mktg & Rec) Join in and follow us Copyright © jobs.ac.uk 1998 - 2026 Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job About Us Contact Us Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job About Us Contact Us Terms of use Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Accessibility Statement Terms of use Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Accessibility Statement Copyright © jobs.ac.uk 1998 - 2026 IE11 Trigger Browser Upgrade Recommended jobs.ac.uk has been optimised for the latest browsers. For the best user experience, we recommend viewing jobs.ac.uk on one of the following:"
