    "https://www.jobs.ac.uk/job/DST425/clinical-fellow-in-counselling": {
      "title": "Clinical Fellow in Counselling",
      "description": "Clinical Fellow in Counselling at The University of Edinburgh This site uses cookies to store information on your computer. Some of these cookies are essential, while others help us to improve your experience by providing insights into how the site is being used. For more detailed information about the cookies we use, please see our Cookie policy I Accept Cookies I Do Not Accept Cookies Necessary Cookies Necessary cookies enable core functionality such as page navigation and access to secure areas. The website cannot function properly without these cookies, and can only be disabled by changing your browser preferences. Functional Cookies These help us to personalise the website to you by remembering your preferences and settings. functional On Off Marketing Cookies Marketing cookies help us provide personalised and relevant services or advertising to our website visitors, and to assess the effectiveness of our marketing campaigns. marketing On Off Analytics Cookies Analytical cookies help us to improve our website by collecting and reporting information on its usage. analytics On Off About this tool (Opens in a new window) Skip to main content Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Recruiters Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Your Account Recruiters Back to search results Clinical Fellow in Counselling The University of Edinburgh - School of Health in Social Science Location: Edinburgh Salary: £41,064 to £48,822\n                                                                                        per annum Hours: Part Time Contract Type: Permanent Placed On: 1st September 2026 Closes: 18th September 2026 Job Ref: 14731 Part Time: 21 hours per week (0.6FTE) Open ended : permanent Use your knowledge to drive change. Be part of something bigger. The University of Edinburgh is a world-class organisation. We look for the best in the field across all disciplines and provide a working environment where academics can develop their careers and passion for their chosen subject area. We offer the full range of academic roles and have a genuine focus on our students performance and wellbeing. The University isn’t just any employer. We are part of a local community and a contributor to global thinking, progress and research. In Edinburgh, you are in one of the world’s most attractive cities with active arts and social sectors, while working in a University that has made significant contributions to society, medicine, physics and teaching for over four centuries. Our people have helped create the modern world and are working on more ground-breaking technologies and practices. The University of Edinburgh invites applications from experienced practitioners for the post of Clinical Fellow in Counselling, Psychotherapy and Applied Social Sciences (CPASS). This role combines clinical leadership, teaching and research within one of the UK's longest-established Counselling and Psychotherapy programmes, dating to the 1970s. The post-holder will play a key role at Hope Park Counselling Centre, the University's COSCA-accredited training placement, which supports 40–50 trainee counsellors and around 120 clients weekly. The role also involves teaching, course organisation and dissertation supervision across our professional programmes, including the full-time Master of Counselling and Doctor of Psychotherapy and Counselling. Role Responsibilities The post-holder will: Support students on placement at Hope Park Counselling Centre, contributing to clinical governance and supervision, and hold a small clinical caseload Deliver core and clinical skills teaching, and act as course organiser for one or more courses Supervise, mark and moderate Masters dissertations and related assessments Develop a personal programme of scholarship and research within CPASS Person Specification Candidates should be: Qualified practitioners with demonstrable experience within the Person-Centred or Psychodynamic tradition Holders of professional accreditation (or eligibility) with COSCA, BACP, UKCP or equivalent Holders of a postgraduate qualification in Counselling and Psychotherapy at Masters or Doctoral level Experience of clinical governance, supervision or teaching in professional counselling education is desirable, as is a record of research or publication in the field. Why Join Us People have always been at the heart of our work. Our people are at the centre of the University community and everything we do. We value colleagues with drive, determination and a passion for what they do. We are a place where everyone is welcome and offer a range of policies and benefits designed to support you in building the right meaningful flexibility that works for you A career with us has a range of other benefits that can be tailored to your lifestyle: Contributing to the work and purpose of the University. Interesting work Professional development and subject matter expertise Apply Before : 18/09/2026, 23:59 Share on social media We value your feedback on the quality of our adverts.\n            If you have a comment to make about the overall quality of this advert,\n            or its categorisation then please send us your feedback Advert information Type / Role: Subject Area(s): Location(s): Job tools Save this job Login to Save Job Max Saved Jobs Reached × Max Saved Jobs Reached A maximum of 500 Saved Jobs can be created against your account. Please remove an existing Saved Job in order to add a new Saved Job. Manage Saved Jobs × Save Job Please sign in or register for an account to save a job. Sign In Register More jobs from The University of Edinburgh Business Support Lead (Health and Wellbeing) Head of Performance Women's Rugby Applications Support Analyst Research Assistant Partnership Manager (AI Scotland) Mechanical Workshop Technician Show all jobs for this employer … More jobs like this Head of School of Psychology Chair in Psychology - Grade 10 Postdoctoral Researcher –Technical (ARIADNE) Lecturer (E&S) (DForenPsy) Teaching Fellow Join in and follow us Copyright © jobs.ac.uk 1998 - 2026 Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job About Us Contact Us Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job About Us Contact Us Terms of use Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Accessibility Statement Terms of use Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Accessibility Statement Copyright © jobs.ac.uk 1998 - 2026 IE11 Trigger Browser Upgrade Recommended jobs.ac.uk has been optimised for the latest browsers. For the best user experience, we recommend viewing jobs.ac.uk on one of the following:"
