    "https://www.jobs.ac.uk/job/DST118/research-assistant-in-net-zero-skills": {
      "title": "Research Assistant in Net-Zero skills",
      "description": "Research Assistant in Net-Zero skills at The University of Edinburgh This site uses cookies to store information on your computer. Some of these cookies are essential, while others help us to improve your experience by providing insights into how the site is being used. For more detailed information about the cookies we use, please see our Cookie policy I Accept Cookies I Do Not Accept Cookies Necessary Cookies Necessary cookies enable core functionality such as page navigation and access to secure areas. The website cannot function properly without these cookies, and can only be disabled by changing your browser preferences. Functional Cookies These help us to personalise the website to you by remembering your preferences and settings. functional On Off Marketing Cookies Marketing cookies help us provide personalised and relevant services or advertising to our website visitors, and to assess the effectiveness of our marketing campaigns. marketing On Off Analytics Cookies Analytical cookies help us to improve our website by collecting and reporting information on its usage. analytics On Off About this tool (Opens in a new window) Skip to main content Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Recruiters Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Your Account Recruiters Back to search results Research Assistant in Net-Zero skills The University of Edinburgh - GeoSciences Location: Edinburgh, Hybrid Salary: £34,610 to £39,906\n                                                                                        per annum Hours: Part Time Contract Type: Fixed-Term/Contract Placed On: 27th August 2026 Closes: 9th September 2026 Job Ref: 14712 Part time: 7 hours per week Fixed term: 15 months The Opportunity: Join an exciting interdisciplinary project exploring how universities can better prepare graduates with the knowledge and skills needed to support the transition to a net-zero future. Funded through the Principal's Teaching Award Scheme (PTAS), this Research Assistant role offers the opportunity to contribute to a high-impact project investigating how net-zero skills can be more effectively embedded across higher education curricula. Working with colleagues from the School of GeoSciences, the Department of Social Responsibility and Sustainability, the Edinburgh Climate Change Institute, the Business School and Edinburgh Napier University, you will help generate evidence that informs curriculum innovation and strengthens links between higher education and industry. The successful candidate will play a central role in designing and delivering mixed-methods research, including: Reviewing current literature and practice relating to the integration of net-zero skills in higher education. Designing and conducting semi-structured interviews with Small and Medium-sized Enterprises (SMEs) to explore industry perspectives on the skills required to support the transition to net zero. Developing and delivering a survey for university staff to identify current practice, opportunities and barriers to embedding net-zero skills within university programmes. Planning and facilitating a collaborative focus group bringing together university staff, students and SME partners to discuss findings and identify practical solutions. Analysing qualitative and quantitative data to produce evidence-based recommendations, case studies, learning resources and a practical net-zero skills framework for wider use across the higher education sector. This role offers an excellent opportunity for an enthusiastic researcher with experience of qualitative and quantitative research methods who is interested in education, sustainability and climate change. You will gain experience working across disciplines and sectors while contributing to the University's ambitions to embed climate and sustainability across learning and teaching. A career with us has a range of other benefits that can be tailored to your lifestyle and ways of working. Apply Before : 09/09/2026, 23:59 Share on social media We value your feedback on the quality of our adverts.\n            If you have a comment to make about the overall quality of this advert,\n            or its categorisation then please send us your feedback Advert information Type / Role: Subject Area(s): Location(s): Job tools Save this job Login to Save Job Max Saved Jobs Reached × Max Saved Jobs Reached A maximum of 500 Saved Jobs can be created against your account. Please remove an existing Saved Job in order to add a new Saved Job. Manage Saved Jobs × Save Job Please sign in or register for an account to save a job. Sign In Register More jobs from The University of Edinburgh Business Support Lead (Health and Wellbeing) Head of Performance Women's Rugby Applications Support Analyst Research Assistant Partnership Manager (AI Scotland) Mechanical Workshop Technician Show all jobs for this employer … More jobs like this Research Associate/Senior Research Associate in Control for Soft Robot Wearable Assistance Postdoctoral Research Associate in Programmable Protein-Templated Materials x4 Post-Doctoral Research Fellow or Researcher Research and Innovation Fellows Post-Doctoral Research Fellow Join in and follow us Copyright © jobs.ac.uk 1998 - 2026 Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job About Us Contact Us Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job About Us Contact Us Terms of use Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Accessibility Statement Terms of use Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Accessibility Statement Copyright © jobs.ac.uk 1998 - 2026 IE11 Trigger Browser Upgrade Recommended jobs.ac.uk has been optimised for the latest browsers. For the best user experience, we recommend viewing jobs.ac.uk on one of the following:"
